# Git workflow

## Branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| `dev` | Integration / development — verified work lands here |
| `main` | Production — **protected**; agents must not push here |

- Feature work on `dev` (Lane S) or `orchestrator/<TASK-ID>` branches (Lane P).
- **Never push** unless the user explicitly asks.
- **Never push to `main`** from agents.

## Commit messages (Conventional Commits)

Subject ≤72 chars, imperative mood, **scoped**. Task commits link work items per `07-phasical-commit-linking.mdc`.

```
feat(<scope>)[#123]: <summary>
fix(<scope>)[#123]: <summary>
chore(<scope>)[P2-01]: <summary>   # roadmap-only when no Phasical mirror
```

**Allowed scopes**: api, web, mobile, shared, infra, docs, roadmap, ci

Plan-file verifier commits: `chore(plan)[#123]: mark P8-07 verified`

Session memory (`.agents/project/agent-memory/`) is **gitignored** — never commit session files.

## DCO sign-off (required)

Every commit must include a `Signed-off-by` trailer per [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Use **`git commit -s`** (or `--signoff`) — never plain `git commit -m` without `-s`.

```bash
git commit -s -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
feat(api)[#42]: add handler

fixes #42
EOF
)"
```

Amend only unpushed commits: `git commit --amend -s --no-edit`. Verifier/orchestrator **FAIL** if a task commit lacks `Signed-off-by`.

## SSH commit signing

This repo expects repo-local `commit.gpgsign=true` with an SSH signing key (see CONTRIBUTING). Cryptographic signing is automatic when configured — agents still use `-s` for DCO. Do not pass `-S` manually when `gpgsign` is enabled.

## Staging

Stage explicit paths only. Never `git add .` or `git add -A`.

## Push policy

Agents default to **local commits only**. Full CI gate before push when user explicitly requests push (see `06-local-ci-before-commit.mdc`).
